Artificial intelligence (AI) is a branch of computer science that builds smart machines capable of performing tasks 
which typically require human intelligence, 
such as learning, reasoning, and problem-solving.
Instead of following rigid rules for every single action, modern AI systems learn by analyzing vast amounts of data to 
find patterns and make independent predictions.
You encounter this technology every day in navigation tools, email spam filters, and digital assistants. 
While AI helps solve major global challenges in medicine and science, it also raises important questions about privacy, job displacement, and ethical use.
